**Alternative: X-Y Scatter Plot with Alliance Vectors**

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Political Agent Skills — Philosophical Position"
        direction LR
        CS["<b>chaos-seize</b><br/>Revolutionary Tactics<br/>Alinsky, Lenin, Mao"]
        CP["<b>civilization-preserve</b><br/>Social Order & Rule of Law<br/>Aristotle, Confucius"]
        BC["<b>burke-conservative</b><br/>Tradition & Gradual Reform<br/>Burke, Kirk"]
        CC["<b>counter-chaos</b><br/>Constitutional Defense<br/>Madison, Tocqueville, Hayek"]
        CS ---|"opposed by"| CP
        CS ---|"countered by"| CC
        BC ---|"allied with"| CP
        BC ---|"allied with"| CC
        CP ---|"allied with"| CC
    end

    classDef chaos fill:#ffcccc,stroke:#cc0000,stroke-width:2px
    classDef preserve fill:#ccffcc,stroke:#00cc00,stroke-width:2px
    
    class CS chaos
    class CP,BC,CC preserve
```

**Usage:** Save this as `assets/skill-taxonomy-diagram.mmd` and render using:
- GitHub (automatic rendering in markdown)
- VS Code with Mermaid extensions
- https://mermaid.live
- `mmdc -i diagram.mmd -o diagram.svg` (Mermaid CLI)
